---
description: schema — YAML loading, resolved scalar/collection/payload/catalog metadata, protocol layouts, legacy template DTOs, and naming helpers.
globs: schema/**/*.go
alwaysApply: false
---

# `schema`

Schema resolution owns shared policy. `LookupScalar` returns scalar metadata by value; `CollectionInfo` resolves element/key identities and native types once, with the existing entity scalar-first versus world custom-first precedence. Catalogs explicitly resolve their declared custom type and optional key into `CatalogInfo`; `ValidateCatalogFile` separately validates raw YAML entries without coercion. Flat DTO fields remain compatibility projections (including empty collection `ProtoType` values used by fingerprints).

`payload.go` shares command/event shorthand, ordered field resolution, and explicit direct-tag validation. Keep command target permissiveness/defaults and event target/entity/`foi_only` validation with their owners. Do not extend payloads to collections or recursive custom types through this extraction.

`ResolveProtoData` is the checked production protocol construction path. `BuildProtoData` keeps its legacy unchecked signature, while `ValidateEnvelopeTags` uses the same allocation and claim validation. `EnvelopeLayout` variants carry ordered message identity, assigned tags and roles, including entity removal. `EntityWireLayout` carries ordered state/delta fields, roles, optionality, owner visibility and original tick dirty-bit indices; revision remains tag 1000. `VarInfo.DeltaPresenceCS` supplies the shared C# nullable-value/reference classification. Do not reconstruct these decisions in emitters.

Treat resolved descriptors and their referenced slices/types as read-only. `WireLayout`, `ProtoWireLayout` and `EnvelopeLayouts` adapt legacy DTOs when resolved metadata is absent: codec dimension zero defaults to two, proto fallback uses root dimensions, and legacy entity tags derive from `UserTag`. Keep these adapters at the generation boundary. Package names, imports, destinations and mutable integration settings do not belong in descriptors.

`visitYAMLDirectory` shares filename-ordered, nonrecursive `.yaml` discovery/read/decode and calls validation immediately per file. Caller policy still owns required/nonempty entities, optional directories and nil/empty results, duplicate-name rules, sorting and diagnostic context. Preserve existing validation strictness: entity/custom fields and world envelope tags must not silently acquire the stricter command/event protobuf range rules.

Optional `protocol_constants` points to a checked YAML catalog loaded by `LoadProtocolConstants`. Set/member names must be canonical snake_case; generated names and authored values must be unique within each set. Values are compile-time integration metadata only: they do not alter protobuf tags or the snapshot schema fingerprint.

Command and event payload fields retain legacy alphabetical numbering when untagged. If any field in a command/event uses `{ tag: N, type: T }`, every field in that payload must use a unique legal direct protobuf tag; entity-targeted commands/events reserve tag 1 for `entity_id`.

**Config, entity, command, and world data definitions:** reads `golem.yaml` (`LoadConfig`), per-entity `.yaml` under the configured `entity_schema` dir (`LoadSchemas`), per-command `.yaml` under the configured `command_schema` dir (`LoadCommands`), and per-world-type `.yaml` under the configured world dir (`LoadWorldSchemas`). Builds `EntityData`, `VarInfo`, `CommandData`, `CommandFieldInfo`, `WorldTypeData`, `WorldFieldInfo`, `WorldUpdateField`, `ProtoTemplateData`, and `SharedData` for generators. Holds **naming helpers** (`ToSnakeCase`, etc.) and **type maps** (proto → Go/TS). Entity var names reserved for metadata (`pos_x`/`pos_y`/`pos_z`/`revision`) and names whose `SnakeToPascal` form is `Server` or `BindServer` (e.g. `server`, `bind_server`, literal `Server`/`BindServer`) are rejected in `BuildEntityData`. Optional entity var `visibility` (`empty`/`all` = public, `owner` = owner-only replication; any other value is a bake error) sets `VarInfo.OwnerOnly`; `EntityData.HasOwnerVars` is true when any var is owner-only. Visibility does not change proto tags or the schema fingerprint. Optional entity `collider` resolves to bake-time `ColliderData` (2D: exactly one of `aabb`/`circle`; 3D: exactly one of `aabb3d`/`sphere`; non-empty `layer`; optional `trigger` default false; positive finite sizes; reject cross-dimension shapes). Optional top-level `collision` (`layers` ≤ 32, symmetric `collides` pairs) resolves via `ResolveCollisionConfig` into `Config.ResolvedCollision` (`yaml:"-"`) at `LoadConfig` and is threaded to `SharedData.Collision` — validate unique non-empty layer names, matrix references, retain self-pairs (e.g. Player/Player), reject duplicate unordered pairs (`[A,B]` and `[B,A]`); collider without `collision:` is a bake error; `collision:` without entity colliders is allowed. Collider/collision metadata is not wire/fingerprint state. Does **not** embed templates, write generated files, or register integrations—that is `codegen/`. Depends only on stdlib + YAML.
